35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The coordination group is empty, but two people write everything by hand. It is too much.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,Half the customer plants have no signal for afternoons. We cannot build on that.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital line is frozen. The software allowance has room, but licences climb per head.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,The last three rollouts failed because everyone had to enter data daily. The narrow tools survived.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,We lose an hour a day copying records. And eleven deliveries were misrouted this year.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, if the capital is frozen, we must use the software allowance carefully.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the developer availability is also bad. They are busy until the third quarter.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, that confirms it. We cannot rely on new builds. We need to use what exists.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, I agree. The standardization efforts failed because they had no owner.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, the copying time is the real cost. We need to stop the duplication.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, the misrouted deliveries are because units hold different addresses. That is a data problem.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, yes. If the data is wrong, the app is useless.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, the fixed-fee work is stable. The licences are not. We should avoid per-head costs.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, the narrow tools for one trade still run. We should pick something narrow.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. The everyday loss is the copying. We need to fix that.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think we need to fix the data first. The coordination group is drowning.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. The network is bad, so a mobile app is risky.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I agree. The budget favors fixed-fee or existing tools.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I agree. The past shows narrow tools survive.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. The copying time is the biggest loss.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
