60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"The candidates are A, B, C, and D. I think C is best. It fixes the data.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Minato. D is risky because of the network. C is safer.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,I agree. C uses the software allowance. It avoids the frozen capital line.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,I agree. C is a narrow tool for data. It fits the pattern of survivors.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,I agree. C stops the copying time. It fixes the misrouted deliveries.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, C is a repository. It does not need new developers.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
